    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see what you're saying about \"systemic success,\" but I'm still a bit nervous. When they ask for the specific \"impact metrics\" of the Pacific project, they usually expect a hard number. If we just talk about \"building trust\" and \"monitoring standards,\" it might look like we're hiding something or that we don't actually have results.\n\nCould you draft a version of that paragraph where we present the results in a way that makes the growth look substantial? Like, instead of saying 5%, could we use language that implies we achieved a significant breakthrough or met the core objectives of the mission? I want a draft that they can read and immediately think, \"Wow, these guys really know how to move the needle.\"",
